  "prediction": "**Deadly Shooting on Las Vegas Strip Leaves Three Dead and Six Injured**\n\nA deadly shooting occurred on the Las Vegas Strip early Thursday morning, leaving three people dead and at least six injured. The incident began with a dispute at an unspecified casino resort, which escalated into a car-to-car shooting. A black Range Rover opened fire on a Maserati, causing it to crash into a taxi, which then burst into flames. The driver of the Maserati, identified as 27-year-old Kenneth Wayne Cherry Jr., was pronounced dead at the scene. The taxi driver, Michael Boldon, and a passenger in the Maserati were also killed.\n\nThe shooting occurred near the intersection of Las Vegas Boulevard and Flamingo Road, a major tourist area. Witnesses described the scene as chaotic, with multiple vehicles involved and a large fire. The incident was described as a \"rolling gun battle\" by some witnesses, but police later clarified that the SUV and Maserati were stopped at a red light when the shooting occurred.\n\nPolice are still investigating the motive behind the shooting, but believe it may have been sparked by an altercation at the casino resort. The Range Rover, which was seen fleeing the scene, was later found abandoned in a nearby parking garage. The SUV's occupants are still at large and are considered armed and dangerous.\n\nThis incident marks the latest in a series of violent incidents on the Las Vegas Strip in recent weeks. Two people were critically wounded in a shooting at a parking garage on February 6, and a tourist was stabbed in an elevator at The Hotel at Mandalay Bay on Saturday.\n\nDespite the recent violence, Las Vegas officials are reassuring tourists that the city remains a safe destination. \"Las Vegas is among the safest travel destinations in the world,\" said Jeremy Handel, a spokesman for the Las Vegas Convention and Visitors Authority. \"While incidents like this are unfortunate, they are rare and do not reflect the overall safety of our city.\"\n\nThe investigation into the shooting is ongoing, with police reviewing surveillance footage and interviewing witnesses. The motive behind the shooting and the identities of the suspects are still unknown.\n\n**Victims and Suspects**\n\n* Kenneth Wayne Cherry Jr., 27, driver of the Maserati, killed in the shooting\n* Michael Boldon, taxi driver, killed in the shooting\n* Passenger in the Maserati, killed in the shooting\n* Suspects: still at large, considered armed and dangerous\n\n**Investigation**\n\n* Police are reviewing surveillance footage and interviewing witnesses\n* The motive behind the shooting is",
